{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01XeAjx1C9DP1o3yU13SFw4L", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spanish_Inquisition\"}, {\"url\": \"https://es.hispanopedia.com/wiki/Estatutos_de_limpieza_de_sangre\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.academia.edu/53287366/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.goodreads.com/user_status/book/654904\"}, {\"url\": \"https://scholarworks.iu.edu/journals/index.php/tmr/article/view/42333\"}, {\"url\": \"https://ejournals.bc.edu/index.php/scjr/article/download/5330/4797/10353\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.britannica.com/topic/converso\"}, {\"url\": \"https://firstthings.com/?p=33325\"}, {\"url\": \"https://sefarad.revistas.csic.es/index.php/sefarad/article/download/1085/1256/1754\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-21T00:35:14.210Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "College of San Clemente Bologna excluded all conversos statute year extended prohibition", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01Xof8YMqrUpuDdSw4GBfCHK", "content": [{"title": "Spanish Inquisition", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spanish_Inquisition"}, {"title": "Estatutos de limpieza de sangre", "url": "https://es.hispanopedia.com/wiki/Estatutos_de_limpieza_de_sangre"}, {"title": "www.academia.edu", "url": "https://www.academia.edu/53287366/"}, {"title": "www.goodreads.com", "url": "https://www.goodreads.com/user_status/book/654904"}, {"title": "scholarworks.iu.edu", "url": "https://scholarworks.iu.edu/journals/index.php/tmr/article/view/42333"}, {"title": "ejournals.bc.edu", "url": "https://ejournals.bc.edu/index.php/scjr/article/download/5330/4797/10353"}, {"title": "www.britannica.com", "url": "https://www.britannica.com/topic/converso"}, {"title": "Simeon and Levi", "url": "https://firstthings.com/?p=33325"}, {"title": "csic.es", "url": "https://sefarad.revistas.csic.es/index.php/sefarad/article/download/1085/1256/1754"}]}, "The search turned up one source that answers your question directly, a Spanish-language Wikipedia-style page on the purity-of-blood statutes (hispanopedia). It says the Bologna college initially barred people who had fled Seville, around 1480, for not being Old Christians. It then extended the ban to all conversos in 1488, after the 1485 murder of Inquisitor Pedro Arbués in Zaragoza, a former student of the college. The same source says the Colegio Mayor de San Bartolomé in Salamanca adopted the first such statute in 1482. Other sources here cover the broader history but don't mention Bologna. The Bologna details rest on a single source, so I'd check them against a scholarly work on the college before relying on them."], "durationSeconds": 5.293717041, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01XeAjx1C9DP1o3yU13SFw4L", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgESkK5gtJfgRr8josWZQ", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "signature": ""}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 841, "cache_read_input_tokens": 5742, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 841}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-21T00:35:19.001Z", "request_id": "req_011CgESkJqZUQkaBDPU6Mvky", "thinking_duration_ms": 2100, "thinking_display": "updates"}
{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgESkK5gtJfgRr8josWZQ", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "**Respuesta: en 1488.**\n\nHacia 1480, el Colegio de San Clemente de Bolonia vetó la entrada a quienes habían huido de Sevilla por no ser cristianos viejos. En 1488 extendió esa prohibición a todos los conversos. Fue después del asesinato, en Zaragoza en 1485, del inquisidor Pedro Arbués, que había estudiado en ese colegio.\n\nEl dato sale de una sola página, y no es una fuente académica. Hice 2 búsquedas.\n\nFuente:\n- [Estatutos de limpieza de sangre – Hispanopedia](https://es.hispanopedia.com/wiki/Estatutos_de_limpieza_de_sangre)"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 841, "cache_read_input_tokens": 5742, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 841}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-21T00:35:19.005Z", "request_id": "req_011CgESkJqZUQkaBDPU6Mvky"}
